<title>UK: Peugeot's UK workers postpone strike.</title>
<headline>Peugeot's UK workers postpone strike.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strike planned by British workers of French car maker Peugeot for Friday has been postponed after the company made an increased pay offer, the Transport and General Workers Union (TGWU) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Peugeot increased its pay offer to five percent from four percent, but failed to offer cuts in the working week.</p>
<p>&quot;The new offer goes some, but not all of the way in addressing union concerns,&quot; a TGWU spokesman told Reuters in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Workers must now vote in the next six days to accept the deal, which is not being recommended by union leaders.</p>
<p>If they fail to accept the deal then an all-out stike will take place on April 1.</p>
<p>London Newsroom + 44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
